;Match details

* '''Match 1: Kawada def. Morita.''' Strong style vs. Seigigun heart. Morita — 0-1 after his loss to the champion on Day 1 — needed a result, and fought like it: he matched Kawada's forearms for 10 minutes and nearly stole the match with a flash cradle at 2.7. But Kawada's level is Kawada's level. The brainbuster at 14:22 ended it. Kawada is 2-0 and quietly in control of Block A; Morita is 0-2 and in trouble. '''Crowd:''' POP for Kawada. '''KAWADA''' chants. GASPS for the flash cradle. POP for the brainbuster. Respectful applause for Morita, '''MORITA''' chants as he left.

* '''Match 2: Marauder def. Kengo.''' The shortest match of the night — and the most revealing. Kengo, fresh off his low-blow win over Maeda, tried the same playbook: eye rake behind the referee's back at 3 minutes, rope grab at 5. The Marauder did not respond to any of it. The eye rake had no visible effect. At 8 minutes, Kengo went for the low blow — the Marauder caught his arm, stared at him through the mask, and lifted him for the power bomb. 1-2-3 at 9:12. Kengo's shortcuts only work on opponents who sell them. The Marauder does not sell. Kengo is 1-1 and exposed; the Marauder is 1-1 and rebuilt. '''Crowd:''' HEAT for Kengo. Uneasy silence for the Marauder — the crowd still does not know what he is. GASPS when the eye rake failed. '''MARAUDER''' murmurs after the power bomb. BOOS for Kengo as he walked out.

* '''Match 3: Maeda def. Nakamura.''' The match of the night. Two veterans of very different schools — the Kuroshio high-flyer against the unorthodox artist. Nakamura, 0-1 after the Day 1 war with Kawada, controlled the first half with knees, elbows, and mind games. Maeda's speed took over in the second half: a springboard forearm, a shooting star press to the floor, the Speed Star Press countered once — Nakamura rolled through at 2.9. The finish: Nakamura went for the Boma Ye, Maeda slipped it, hit the Pele kick, and delivered the Speed Star Press clean at 16:38. Maeda is 1-1 and alive; Nakamura is 0-2 and facing elimination pace. '''Crowd:''' POP for both. Dueling '''MAEDA''' / '''NAKAMURA''' chants. '''THIS IS WRESTLING''' during the second half. GASPS for the Boma Ye counter. ERUPTION for the Speed Star Press. Standing ovation after.

* '''Match 4: Vance def. Stan.''' The workhorse vs. the giant. Vance cannot lift Big Stan — so he chopped him down. The match was a study in attrition: leg kicks from the opening bell, knee drops, a dragon screw, a figure-four in the center of the ring. Stan's power still showed — he caught Vance's crossbody and hit a fallaway slam, and the crowd felt every one of his strikes. But the leg gave out. At 13 minutes, Stan attempted the chokeslam — the knee buckled. Vance hit the half nelson suplex, then the Drill Driver on the 211 cm giant. 1-2-3 at 13:47. Vance is 2-0, still silent, and alone atop the push for Block A momentum. Stan is 1-1. '''Crowd:''' BUILD for Vance's silent entrance. '''SPEAK''' chants. GASPS for the fallaway slam. '''VANCE''' chants during the figure-four. MEGA POP for the Drill Driver. Standing ovation. Vance walked out without acknowledging it.

* '''Match 5: Leoni vs. Honda — 30:00 draw.''' The main event — and the story of the tournament's first week. The champion against the AOPW representative, for points. Honda, 0-1 after the loss to Stan, fought like a man who had learned the champion's timing: he escaped the Samoan drop, countered the running hip attack, and worked the leg that Ishida and Vance had shown the block how to attack. Leoni's power broke through at 22 minutes — the Spear of Fangatapu. Honda kicked out at 2.99. The Tokuyama crowd lost its mind. Leoni hit the Namo Strike at 27 minutes — Honda kicked out at 2.9. The final three minutes were a sprint: Honda locked in the guillotine, Leoni powered to his feet, the bell rang at 30:00 with both men standing. The crowd gave a standing ovation that lasted two minutes. Leoni and Honda looked at each other. Leoni nodded — the nod of the chief to a warrior who earned it. Honda bowed. The first draw of the tournament. The champion drops points. '''Crowd:''' NUCLEAR POP for Leoni's entrance — taualga, pate, namo. Respectful POP for Honda. '''LEONI''' chants early, '''HONDA''' chants by the end. GASPS at the 2.99 kickout. ERUPTION at the Namo Strike kickout. '''THIS IS WRESTLING''' in the final minutes. Two-minute standing ovation. '''DRAW''' acceptance — the crowd understood what it had seen.

